WEBVTT

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.910
Looks like the party's getting started.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.380
Madame Ch'en, this is Amiya.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.280
We've found Misha.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.170
<i>Understood.</i>

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.640
<i>I'll send you the rendezvous location. Escort the target there immediately.</i>

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.660
I understand—

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.400
<i>The L.G.D. will make sure the 
rendezvous point is safe. Over.</i>

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.140
U-Um...

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.000
She's just treating us as her servants.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.850
Looks like this partnership is in name only.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.440
Let's hurry to the rendezvous point.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.860
She said the L.G.D. will 
make sure it's safe there.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.080
Misha?

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.890
So you were planning to hand me over 
to the L.G.D. from the very beginning?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:49.890
Oh, no, it's just that the L.G.D. asked us to 
take you into protective custody. It's not...

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:55.890
I'm such an idiot.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.910
I almost believed you.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:04.180
I really want to help you!

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.050
And I'm going to negotiate with 
the L.G.D. to let Rhodes Island

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.240
protect you and the other Infected!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.290
There's no way they'll agree to that.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.390
If you were here to take me in,

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.550
you could've just said so 
instead of lying to me.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:26.560
That's not it! We aren't trying
 to capture you! Though...

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:32.550
Sorry. I guess that doesn't 
really make a difference to you.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:37.780
But you can't outrun them
for too much longer, can you?

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.370
Given the circumstances,

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:42.990
I think you'd be better off accepting
 the L.G.D.'s protection for now.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.450
Put your faith in Amiya.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.500
Hello!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.420
I missed you guys so much!

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:00.530
Exusiai!

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.170
Hey there, Amiya!

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.000
I gotcha, didn't I?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.570
Yes, you really did!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.610
Yeah!

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:12.160
What are you doing here? Don't you 
have work to do at Penguin Logistics?

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:13.100
Hey.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.030
Well, yeah, but I thinks things 
are about to get pretty hectic.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:21.830
Not sure why, but lots of menacing-looking
 men are zoning in on this location.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:22.710
Huh?!

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:27.850
Every route out of the slums
 is swarming with hostiles.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.030
Hostiles?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:34.790
Probably the Reunion fighters 
and Infected hiding in the slums.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.240
It wouldn't be all that strange
 for the slum dwellers

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.630
to take Reunion's side when 
they've been oppressed for so long.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:47.640
Whatever the case, we have to get 
out of here and get Misha to safety.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.490
Watch out!

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:55.890
Those are Arts!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.590
They brought Casters with them, huh?

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.450
Take care of the Doctor and Misha!

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.700
Okay!

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.530
Getting in on the action, huh?

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.200
So that's Reunion?

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.540
Out of my way.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.250
This way!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.180
After her!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:24.920
Reunion's after Misha, too?

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.630
Misha!

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.350
I won't let you.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.620
Okay. Got 'em all.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:54.120
Oh, man! Beautifully done! Good work.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.120
You should be helping out, too.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.130
Are you hurt?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.300
Are you okay, Misha?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:16.810
I'm fine.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:20.810
What was that about?
 It's like they were waiting for us.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.650
Hey, looks like we've got more company.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.950
That was fast.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.260
What do we do, little bunny?

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:34.410
I want to avoid fighting if possible.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:38.080
But how do we find a safe route out?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.390
All righty! At times like this, 
you can count on me!

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:44.500
I know a secret way out that 
the enemies will never suspect.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.670
Really?!

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.860
Yup. Though I'll have 
to check if it's safe first.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.920
For now, head on over there.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:54.640
Okay!

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.780
All right, see you in a bit.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.820
Be careful!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.650
Let's go, everyone.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.320
Misha?

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.890
Take my hand.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.270
Thanks.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:47.690
We're almost at the place 
Exusiai told us about.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.570
Misha, can you walk that far?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.030
Yeah.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:53.820
Let's go.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.420
Stand back.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:34.400
Huh?!

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.030
You took your time.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:40.910
Texas!

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.010
Want some?

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.270
Thanks, but no.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.420
All right, then.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.810
What happened here?

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:49.920
We had guests.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.850
But why are you here?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:55.820
Exusiai called me.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.680
Wow, guess she can be pretty 
thoughtful, every now and then.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.100
It seems these Reunion guys have 
a lot of reinforcements at their disposal.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:11.110
They were still underground not long ago, 
but they're out in the open in large groups now.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:18.160
I knew it. Reunion is using the slums 
to build their influence inside Lungmen.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.210
Also...

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.130
They might be after Misha.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.230
Me? Why?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.630
We don't know why either.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:34.210
It's probably something that only 
Lungmen and Reunion know about.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:39.830
Well, we just have to go give our captain's
 cheek a little poke later to find out.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.890
Exusiai's made sure the route is secure.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.200
Let's go.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.910
Everyone, find cover!

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:00.200
Doctor!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.450
Over here!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.760
They've got us pinned down.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.870
I don't like it when they get the jump on us.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.290
Where is... everyone?

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.060
There you are.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.050
Misha.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:06.360
That voice...

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:26.910
Fall back!

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:28.160
This way.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:33.390
Wait!

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.060
You're just gonna let them go?

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:37.210
Of course not.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:40.710
This day has finally come.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:53.270
Hey, is there a way out up there?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.860
We can't let them catch up to us.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:12:01.000
"Do whatever you need to do 
to get to your destination."

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.320
That's one of Penguin Logistics' mottos.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:06.030
Like... <i>anything</i>?

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:17.880
Hey!

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.630
This way! This way!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.300
Hey!

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:24.550
Guys, we're gonna jump from here!

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.160
Jump?

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:29.680
U-Um... Surely you don't mean...

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.650
jumping over there?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.480
Yeah! Bingo!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.450
There's no way anybody
 would expect this, right?

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.610
It's downright perfect, isn't it?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.370
They're here!

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.280
Come on now. How is any of this perfect?

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:52.000
Well, I wasn't expecting this.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.970
Texas, how come you 
didn't take them all out?

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.800
You didn't ask me to go that far.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.210
All right, in that case, 
guess we've got no other choice!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.340
She jumped it...

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.160
Hurry, all of you!

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:13.560
For real?

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.900
I'll hold the enemies here! Go on ahead!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.720
Jeez!

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:21.360
Roger!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.620
Doctor, go on ahead, please!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:29.990
Misha!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.050
Doctor, hold on tight, 'kay?

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:43.090
You aren't going anywhere!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.610
Damn you.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:14.620
Sorry, but this route is just for us!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:17.840
Misha...

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:32.890
We're almost at the rendezvous point
 where Officer Ch'en is waiting for us.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.770
What a journey this has been.

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.280
Misha?!

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.400
She looks pale.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.450
I'm just... feeling a little dizzy.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.410
It's okay.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.290
Let's take a break.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:04.580
Huh? You're kidding me! 
We're almost at our destination!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.670
I want to ask you something.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:17.590
What is it?

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.520
What is Reunion?

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.150
They're a group of Infected.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.690
Two groups of Infected 
are fighting each other?

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:30.370
Why?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.200
Because the paths we chose are different.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.950
How?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:42.170
Reunion claims they're creating 
a place the Infected can call home.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:50.670
But that also means they'll kill all non-Infected,
 and any who oppose their ideals.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:58.740
But Rhodes Island is seeking a way for 
the Infected and non-Infected to coexist.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.110
That's what you're doing?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.690
Yes.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:09.310
As we have both chosen different paths 
for ourselves, conflict is unavoidable.

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.690
As pathetic as that sounds.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:17.700
I... I don't know what happened.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:23.710
All of a sudden, it went crazy on the streets
 of Chernobog, like a war had broken out.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:28.210
I was so scared. 
I didn't know what was going on.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.810
All I could do was run.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:39.740
It was Reunion who attacked Chernobog.

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:41.980
I see...

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.980
Misha, how long have you been here?

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.180
About a week, maybe.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.480
A week?

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:59.850
After I got to Lungmen, I found out 
this was growing. And then...

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.750
Misha! Hang in there!

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.020
Oripathy symptoms...

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.460
So soon?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:11.700
There's both acute and chronic Oripathy.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.540
This is only an emergency treatment.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:32.840
If we don't get you thorough 
treatment as soon as possible...

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.160
Amiya...

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:43.830
Misha, we'll ask Lungmen to let us take you
 back to Rhodes Island for treatment.

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.910
Anyway, let's hurry.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.280
So cramped...

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:04.330
What am I supposed to do?

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.600
This is the shortest route!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.060
Hey, look, everyone! Once we're 
through here, we're at our destination!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.110
Get bent!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.720
This is our turf!

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.740
Leave now!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:20.120
Stop this! We're all Infected here!
 We don't want to fight!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.120
You should come with us!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:25.150
They destroyed our homes!

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:26.500
Wake up already!

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:30.240
Come with us and stand up for the Infected!

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:33.460
What are you talking about?
Give us back our homes!

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.820
What should we do, Amiya?

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:44.310
Let's take this chance to slip 
past them and out of the slums!

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:47.310
Get out of the way!

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.100
Piss off!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.670
Go, Amiya.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.940
I'm okay.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:08.220
I'll be quick.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:10.010
Yeah.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:14.800
Doctor, please take care of Misha.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:15.960
Sure.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.120
I knew I made the right 
choice coming with you.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.470
All right! Let's teach 
these bastards a lesson!

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.070
Aw, dang. So it's come to this, huh?

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.630
You knew it would, didn't you?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.480
Guess so.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.490
It's time you settled down!

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.710
All right, there we go!

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.840
It's dangerous here.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:11.890
Hurry up and leave this place.

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:13.970
Leave?

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:18.890
Where are we supposed to go?

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:23.400
This... This is our home.

00:20:24.440 --> 00:20:29.910
Even if they tear down the whole place,
 we have nowhere else to go.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:37.100
I'm sorry.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:48.470
Those Reunion punks. They dare call 
themselves the "saviors" of the Infected?

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.630
Bunch of liars.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:54.950
Even so, there are those who buy their story.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.130
Really makes me wonder why.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:01.690
And they don't buy Rhodes Island's at all.

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:11.200
Reunion makes it feel like all the 
Infected's dreams could actually come true.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:17.870
If they can look away from the harsh reality 
for even a moment and be saved from it,

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:20.550
it doesn't matter if it's all a fantasy.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:24.720
The harsher the reality, the more 
they want something to hold onto.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:30.720
But Rhodes Island will never lie about 
being able to do something they can't.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.640
The Infected are trapped in their fantasies.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:41.440
There's no way they'd believe a little bunny 
girl who can't flatter them, or tell them lies.

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:50.490
I believe her.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.000
I believe Amiya.

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.150
Misha...

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.480
Thank you.
